<!--
    The mark, as specified in the Brand section of
    `docs/design/redesign-variants.html`: a level meter whose tallest bar is a
    bookmark. The notch reads as both a ribbon tail and a peak, which is the
    whole app in one silhouette — save a link, hear it read back — rather than
    a bookmark that says nothing about the listening or a waveform that says
    nothing about the saving.

    It replaces three fanned bookmark ribbons whose fault was scale rather than
    concept: that artwork occupied about 15% of its canvas and dissolved into a
    speck at launcher size. This fills roughly 70%.

    Terracotta, not the mockup's cyan — the migration kept two palettes,
    terracotta and monochrome, and never adopted the "signature" accent. The
    three bars step down in alpha off the bookmark, so the accent is one colour
    at four weights and not four colours.

    Geometry is the mockup's own, shifted 2 units left so the mark centres on
    the canvas, and held inside the 66-unit safe zone by the outer group's
    scale. Both consumers crop: a launcher masks the outer third of an adaptive
    icon, and the Android 12+ splash shows the inner two thirds of its icon.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <group
        android:name="mark"
        android:pivotX="54"
        android:pivotY="54"
        android:scaleX="0.85"
        android:scaleY="0.85">

        <!--
            Each bar is its own group so the splash can animate it. The pivot
            is the row's centre line, which every bar is already centred on, so
            a bar grows out of the middle rather than up off a baseline.
        -->
        <group
            android:name="bar_a"
            android:pivotX="24.5"
            android:pivotY="54">
            <path
                android:fillAlpha="0.45"
                android:fillColor="#C6684A"
                android:pathData="M20,44.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 9,0 v19 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -9,0 z" />
        </group>

        <group
            android:name="bar_b"
            android:pivotX="39.5"
            android:pivotY="54">
            <path
                android:fillAlpha="0.7"
                android:fillColor="#C6684A"
                android:pathData="M35,34.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 9,0 v39 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -9,0 z" />
        </group>

        <!-- The peak: a bookmark rather than a fourth bar. -->
        <path
            android:fillColor="#C6684A"
            android:pathData="M50,24 h20 a3,3 0 0 1 3,3 v57 l-13,-10 l-13,10 V27 a3,3 0 0 1 3,-3 z" />

        <group
            android:name="bar_c"
            android:pivotX="83.5"
            android:pivotY="54">
            <path
                android:fillAlpha="0.55"
                android:fillColor="#C6684A"
                android:pathData="M79,40.5 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 9,0 v27 a4.5,4.5 0 0 1 -9,0 z" />
        </group>
    </group>
</vector>
